course: dictionary
lesson: 10050
title: What is a territory?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A territory is an area that belongs to someone, or that an animal lives in and guards. Look at the clues around the word. «Gulls have many calls; the loud long call with the head thrown back claims a territory.» Claims tells you the gull is saying the area is its own.
explain: Territory can also mean a special part of a country. Australia has the Northern Territory. It has its own government, but it is not a full state. Look for clues like «part of a country» or «its own government» to help you.
explain: Territory can mean new ideas or experiences too. «New territory» means something you have not done or learned before. Ask yourself: what would fit here? If the sentence is about learning something new, the meaning is probably new ideas.
fact: A territory is an area of land.
fact: Animals such as robins, lions and wolves mark and defend their territory.
fact: «The laughing kookaburra» is a big kingfisher whose family groups laugh together at dawn and dusk to mark territory.
fact: «Foxes scream at night» to mark territory, and people sometimes mistake the sound for a person screaming.
fact: Territory can also mean an area of knowledge or experience, as in «new territory».
exercise: «Gulls have many calls; the loud long call with the head thrown back claims a territory.» What does claims mean here? | Flies away from the area | Gives the area away | *Says the area is theirs | Sings quietly to a friend
exercise: The Northern Territory is a part of a country with its own government, but it is not a full state. Which country is it in? | *Australia | Canada | Britain | Scotland
exercise: Ella says territory just means a map. What is a better meaning for an animal's territory? | A type of plant that grows in the sea | A loud noise made at dawn | A tiny insect that bites | *The area an animal lives in and defends from others
test: «In spring male songbirds such as blackbirds sing at dawn to claim territory and be noticed.» Why do the blackbirds sing? | *To claim their area and be noticed | To get a free meal | To learn how to fly | To sleep better at night
test: Maya says, «When I started coding, I was in new territory.» What does new territory mean here? | A place with a map | A kind of bird song | *Something she had not done or known before | A computer game for two players
exam: Which of these is a territory? | A long sentence in a book | A fast kind of car | *A part of Australia with its own government, like the Northern Territory | A type of bird song
